          %h2#exposition_of_higher_gauge_theories_as_models
            Exposition of higher gauge theories as
            = succeed "-models" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
          %p
            We discuss how
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theories"} gauge theories
            and their higher analogs are naturally regarded as
            = succeed "-models." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
          %h3#HigherGeometricTargetSpaces Higher geometric target spaces
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model+--+exposition+of+classical+sigma-models"} classical sigma-models
            all have
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \geq 2
            on, the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+gauge+field"} background gauge field
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} with connection
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+an+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} ∞-connections
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            of such higher smooth bundles is no longer in general a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 2
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-groupoid"} Lie 2-groupoid
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 3
            and eventually generally a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoid
          %p
            This means that – unless we would artifically treat the total space of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+gauge+field"} background gauge field
            bundle on different grounds than its base space – the general theory of
            = succeed "-models" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
          %p
            At least from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 2
            on, for instance, target spaces should be allowed to be
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+groupoid"} proper
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+groupoid"} étale
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"}> orbifold
                s
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string"} string
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifold"} orientifold
            background gauge fields mentioned
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/sigma-model+--+exposition+of+classical+sigma-models#RelativisticString"} before
            involve in general a
            = succeed "-orbifold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
          %p
            But once we pass to the higher geometry of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            there is its
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            Lie groupoid, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
            of the trivial action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on the point, which we shall write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{B}G := *//G
                  \\,;
          %p
            and this can perfectly serve as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            object for
            = succeed "-models" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G \in Top
            of the Lie group. In fact, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G
            gives
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+class"} isomorphism class
            of smooth
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            also remembers the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"} automorphism
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of smooth
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            we have that the
            %em groupoid
            of morphisms of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \to \mathbf{B}G
            (the
            %em correct
            morphisms, sometimes called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morita+morphism"} Morita morphism
            to distinguish them from any incorrect notion) is that of smooth
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SmoothGrpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi G
                  %mi Bund
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  SmoothGrpd(\Sigma, \mathbf{B}G) \simeq G Bund(\Sigma) \in Grpd
                  \\,,
          %p
            whereas the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G \simeq \vert \mathbf{B}G\vert
            only sees the equivalence classes:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi G
                  %mi Bund
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Set
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\Sigma, B G] \simeq \pi_0 G Bund(\Sigma) \in Set
                  \\,.
          %p
            This indicates that (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"}> nonabelian
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            should have a formulation as a
            = succeed "-model" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            the Lie groupoid
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = \mathbf{B}G
            = succeed "-model" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \to X = \mathbf{B}G
            is a
            = succeed "-bundle," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
            of
            = succeed "-bundles." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            But a field configuration in
            = succeed "-gauge" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is not just a
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth groupoid
            that does:
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi conn
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{conn}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+of+Lie+algebra+valued+1-forms"} groupoid of Lie algebra valued 1-forms
          %p
            Here by a
            %em smooth groupoid
            we mean a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            that comes with a rule for which of its collections of objects or morphisms are
            = succeed "." do
              %em smoothly parameterized families
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-sheaf"} (2,1)-sheaf
            or
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} diffeological groupoid
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+sheaf"} concrete
            objects. While it is useful to know if a given smooth groupoid is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+sheaf"} concrete
            or even
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            exists for general smooth
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-models," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
          %p
            The non-concrete smooth groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{conn}
            that we just mentioned is defined by the following rule: for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            = succeed "-parameterized" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+valued+1-form"} valued differential 1-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \Omega^1(U, \mathfrak{g})
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
